    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining the offensive unit at a 74.56 efficiency score. Benefiting from a prime 14% park boost and a favorable dynamic platoon split against Hughes, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is our most reliable engine for power and average. **Kyle Tucker** (71.33) and **Jacob Wilson** (70.97) follow closely; **Kyle Tucker** leverages elite BvP history against Nola to offset a tough matchup, while **Jacob Wilson** benefits significantly from a soft 5.31 xERA opponent, making him an ideal top-of-the-order producer. **Drake Baldwin** rounds out the top tier at 67.31, with his leadoff role and high xwOBA cementing his status as a high-floor start despite a moderate SP_xERA for King.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Nasim Nunez**, who finished with a 55.36, falling just short of the efficiency threshold required to displace **Cole Carrigg** (55.40) or **Jackson Merrill** (57.35). While **Nasim Nunez** gained from a massive park boost, his #9 batting order position dragged his aggregate score below our active outfielders. Conversely, **Gunnar Henderson** remains in the lineup despite a sub-60 score (58.50) because his underlying base projection and leadoff/top-of-order upside remain superior to the alternatives on the bench. We are tracking a moderate risk with **Coby Mayo** (60.25); while his score is bolstered by a speed-friendly delivery from Bennett, any weather shifts in that venue could quickly drop him into the marginal tier. Otherwise, the lineup is optimized to maximize stolen base potential without sacrificing our core R/RBI production.",
